%N A398428 Number of P-partitions of n where P is the labeled poset defined by a covers b if f(a) > f(b) where f(i) = floor(sqrt(2*i) + 1/2).
%C A398428 The structure of P shown below:
%C A398428   ...
%C A398428  4 5 6
%C A398428   3 2
%C A398428    1
%C A398428 Every element in P covers all elements in the row beneath it and is covered by all elements in the row above. Specifically the partitions counted here are p-partitions over some order ideal of P. Because P is similar to the 2-d integer lattice but with additional covering relations these partitions can be represented as restricted plane partitions as shown in the example.
%H A398428 John Tyler Rascoe, <a href="/A398428/a398428_1.txt">PARI code</a>.
%F A398428 a(n) <= A000219(n).
%e A398428 a(4) = 9: 4   3 1   3   2 2   2   2 1   1 1   1 1   1 1 1.
%e A398428                     1         2   1     1     1 1   1
